      "content": "The void you feel isn't a destination; it's a reflection of how much you've been hollowed out. Trying to find a \"real you\" when you feel like nothing is like trying to fill a bottomless pit. Instead of fighting the emptiness, maybe you could just let it be a quiet, undeniable truth. Sometimes, the only way to stop the constant, exhausting performance is to just stop trying to be anything at all.",
